isp-tools for Debian
=====================

PHP Autoloader
--------------

This package uses the **Debian PHP autoloader system** (pkg-php-tools) with a
static autoloader committed in the repository as `debian/autoload.php`
(no `phpab` run and no Composer at build or install time).

Classes are installed in: `/usr/share/php/isp-tools/SpojeNet/`
Autoloader: `/usr/share/php/isp-tools/autoload.php`
Registration: `/usr/share/pkg-php-tools/autoloaders/isp-tools`

To use in your PHP code:

```php
require_once '/usr/share/php/isp-tools/autoload.php';
```

**Note:** This package does NOT ship `vendor/autoload.php` from Composer.
Use the Debian autoloader instead for proper system integration.

MultiFlexi application definitions
----------------------------------

Package `multiflexi-isp-tools` installs the application definitions to
`/usr/share/isp-tools/multiflexi/*.app.json` and their icons (named by the
application UUID) to the shared `/usr/share/multiflexi/images/`.
Package `isp-tools` ships the application icon `isp-tools.svg`
(`/usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/`) and the AppStream metainfo
`io.github.spoje_net.isp_tools.metainfo.xml`.

Installation
------------

For Debian, Ubuntu & friends please use repo:

```shell
sudo apt install lsb-release wget
echo "deb http://repo.vitexsoftware.cz $(lsb_release -sc) main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/vitexsoftware.list
sudo wget -O /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/vitexsoftware.gpg http://repo.vitexsoftware.cz/keyring.gpg
sudo apt update
sudo apt install isp-tools
```

Composer Integration
--------------------

If using Composer in your application, you can reference the Debian package:

```json
{
    "require": {
        "deb/isp-tools": "*"
    },
    "repositories": [
        {
            "type": "path",
            "url": "/usr/share/php/isp-tools",
            "options": {
                "symlink": true
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

Migration from Composer vendor/autoload.php
--------------------------------------------

If you're migrating from Composer's autoloader, replace:

```php
require_once __DIR__ . '/../vendor/autoload.php';
```

with:

```php
require_once '/usr/share/php/isp-tools/autoload.php';
```

This ensures you're using the system-wide Debian packages instead of bundled dependencies.

